WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.345 --> 00:00:02.017
(Cuban dance music)

00:00:02.017 --> 00:00:03.800
- [Kadir Lopez Nieves] Walking
through the city of Havana,

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.967
one day I look up, and one of
the oldest neon signs was off.

00:00:08.929 --> 00:00:11.656
I realized I should just
do something with it.

00:00:11.656 --> 00:00:14.434
I do see the future of
the beauty of the city

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:18.601
related with the past, and
that past was the neon.

00:00:34.925 --> 00:00:37.111
- [Narrator] Cuban
artist Kadir López Nieves

00:00:37.111 --> 00:00:39.790
is bringing new light and
life to the streets of Havana

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.673
by restoring the city's
neon signs one-by-one

00:00:42.673 --> 00:00:45.315
with his project, Havana Light.

00:00:45.315 --> 00:00:48.420
Many of these signs have
sat abandoned for decades.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.703
- [Kadir] In the '50s and '40s,

00:00:49.703 --> 00:00:52.444
there was the renaissance
of the neon in Cuba,

00:00:52.444 --> 00:00:55.933
thousands of neon all
over the city of Havana.

00:00:55.933 --> 00:00:58.134
The neon was part of the architecture.

00:00:58.134 --> 00:01:00.154
- [Narrator] But in the
1960s, the neon signs

00:01:00.154 --> 00:01:03.591
became difficult and expensive
to maintain, and slowly

00:01:03.591 --> 00:01:07.758
they were taken down or
shut off and left to decay.

00:01:11.702 --> 00:01:13.908
- [Kadir] Today, the neon is considered

00:01:13.908 --> 00:01:16.183
like a piece of art in itself.

00:01:16.183 --> 00:01:18.654
The mission is taking the art outside.

00:01:18.654 --> 00:01:20.063
People walking in the
street, they don't have to be

00:01:20.063 --> 00:01:23.497
into the museum to look
into a piece of art.

00:01:23.497 --> 00:01:25.714
- [Narrator] Over the past
three years, Kadir and his team

00:01:25.714 --> 00:01:29.748
have restored dozens of
signs across the city.

00:01:29.748 --> 00:01:32.169
It can be a painstaking process.

00:01:32.169 --> 00:01:34.791
- It's no different
than fixing an old car.

00:01:34.791 --> 00:01:37.049
You take all the elements
out and you start

00:01:37.049 --> 00:01:40.716
fixing everything that
is rusted or damaged.

00:01:41.642 --> 00:01:43.673
The most difficult thing is the bending.

00:01:43.673 --> 00:01:47.840
It's a skill that very few
people have in the world.

00:01:49.115 --> 00:01:51.999
So, the most complicated
process is taking it down

00:01:51.999 --> 00:01:55.334
and lifting it up, 'cause
you need a lot of men.

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:56.989
Certain places like Old
Havana, you gotta do it

00:01:56.989 --> 00:01:59.376
by rope, by hand, because big cars

00:01:59.376 --> 00:02:02.459
and cranes, they cannot get in there.

00:02:09.355 --> 00:02:12.899
It is phenomenal to see
the people's reaction.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.812
In some cases, we see kind
of tears in their eyes.

00:02:15.812 --> 00:02:17.993
They get so excited about seeing something

00:02:17.993 --> 00:02:22.221
that was about to disappear
coming back to life.

00:02:22.221 --> 00:02:23.737
Neon ...

00:02:23.737 --> 00:02:26.641
it means a restoration ...

00:02:26.641 --> 00:02:27.511
of hope.

00:02:27.511 --> 00:02:30.035
You make people's lives happier.

00:02:30.035 --> 00:02:32.952
There's nothing stronger than that.

